doc ///
  Key
    (bFunction, Ideal, List)
  Headline
    $b$-function of an ideal
  Usage
    b = bFunction(I, w)
  Inputs
    I:Ideal
      a holonomic ideal in the Weyl algebra $D$
    w:List
      a list of integer weights corresponding to the differential variables in the Weyl algebra
  Outputs
    b:RingElement
      a polynomial $b(s)$ which is the $b$-function of $I$ with respect to $w$
  Description
    Text
      Use @TO "setHomSwitch"@(true) to force all the subroutines
      to use homogenized @TO "WeylAlgebra"@.

      @BOLD "Definition."@ The $b$-function $b(s)$
      is defined as the monic generator
      of the intersection of $in_{(-w,w)}(I)$ and $K[s]$,
      where $s = w_1 t_1 + \cdots + w_n t_n$
      (here $t_i = x_i D_i$).
    Example
      R = QQ[x_1,x_2,D_1,D_2,WeylAlgebra=>{x_1=>D_1,x_2=>D_2}]
      I = ideal(x_1, D_2-1)
      bFunction(I,{1, 0})
  Caveat
    The ring of $I$ should not have any parameters:
    it should be a pure Weyl algebra. Similarly, this ring
    should not be a homogeneous @TO "WeylAlgebra"@.
  SeeAlso
    globalBFunction
    factorBFunction
///

