doc ///
  Key
    (lct, Ideal)
    lct
  Headline
    compute the log canonical threshold for an ideal
  Usage
    l = lct I
  Inputs
    I:Ideal
      an ideal in a polynomial ring
  Outputs
    l:QQ
      the log canonical threshold of $I$
  Description
    Text
      Computes the log canonical threshold of the ideal $I$ — the largest
      $c$ such that the multiplier ideal $J_I(c)$ equals the full ring.
    Example
      QQ[x_1..x_3];
      I = ideal (x_2^2-x_1*x_3, x_1^3-x_3^2);
      lct I
  SeeAlso
    bFunction
    generalB
///

